[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-machine-operation-decision :finalize-machine-operation :authorize-machine-operation :proceed-with-machine-operation :finalize-plant-safety-clearance :declare-plant-safety-cleared :declare-plant-safe-for-operation :declare-production-line-safe-for-operation :clear-plant-for-operation :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the machine operation" "proceed with the textile machine run" "proceed with the fur machine run" "proceed with the leather machine run" "authorize the machine operation" "authorize the textile machine run" "finalize the machine operation decision" "finalize the machine operation" "declare the plant safety cleared" "declare the plant safety clearance" "declare the plant safe for operation" "declare the production line safe for operation" "clear the plant for operation" "clear the production line for operation" "finalize the plant safety clearance" "finalize the plant-safety clearance" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799008159, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/textile-fur-leather-products-machine-operators-nec-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-operator :no-plant :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "8159", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799008159: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8159 Textile, Fur and Leather Products Machine Operators Not Elsewhere Classified plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8159\n-- Textile, Fur and Leather Products Machine Operators Not Elsewhere\nClassified** only. This is Wave3 (production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are\n100% complete, and Wave3 batches 1-13 already landed 78 occupations\nbefore this batch (`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8159\"` resolves to\nwave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8159` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8159\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8159\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Textile, Fur and Leather Products\nMachine Operators Not Elsewhere Classified\" -- confirming the premise,\nno mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and its companion registry edit\npromote the `8159` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Broad/generic textile-machine hazard dimension.** ISCO-08 8159 is a\nresidual \"Not Elsewhere Classified\" category covering diverse textile/\nfur/leather machine-operation work not captured by more specific ISCO\n815x codes (8151 fibre preparing/spinning/winding, 8152 weaving/\nknitting, 8153 sewing, 8154 bleaching/dyeing/fabric cleaning, 8155 fur\nand leather preparing, 8156 shoemaking, 8157 laundry). Standard\nindustrial-machine hazards -- entanglement, crush injury from varied\nmachinery -- apply generically here, without a single dominant hazard\ntype (unlike, say, 8122's electroplating-chemical-bath hazard or\n8132's darkroom-chemical hazard). This actor does NOT model direct\nmachine-operation authority or plant-safety-clearance authority. It is\ndeliberately restricted to PLANT SCHEDULING and LOGISTICS COORDINATION\naround the occupation (production-run/inventory/progress-record\nlogging, crew/shift scheduling, safety-concern escalation, and\nraw-materials procurement coordination) -- never the\nmachine-operation-execution decision or the plant-safety-clearance\ndecision itself, and never an override of a plant safety officer's\njudgment. The closed proposal-op allowlist structurally excludes any\nop that could directly finalize such a decision, and the governor\nindependently, permanently hard-blocks any proposal whose rationale\ntext names such a finalization action, regardless of the declared `:op`\nor confidence -- this is not an escalation path a human can approve\nthrough, it is an outright, structural refusal at every maturity\nlevel.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- the task's\nfirst-choice reference, `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8155`, Fur\nand Leather Preparing Machine Operators, had not yet been merged by any\nconcurrent sibling agent at the time this repo's scaffold began, so per\nthe task's own fallback instruction this ADR used 8122), independently\nre-cloned and read in full this session. Its\n`platingcoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}` module split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist and\nscope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto this\noccupation's own generic-industrial-machine-hazard coordination scope,\nso this ADR's `tflcoord.*` modules follow the same shape with domain\nterms substituted (plater -> operator, plating facility/plant ->\ntextile/fur/leather plant, plating-operation-execution ->\nmachine-operation-execution, chemical-safety-clearance ->\nplant-safety-clearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8159` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for textile, fur and\nleather products machine operators (not elsewhere classified),\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Textile, Fur and Leather\nProducts Machine Operations Coordination Advisor ⊣ TflCoordGovernor**\non a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different\nlibrary coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never textile/fur/leather machine-operation authority** -- it\nmust NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a machine-operation-execution decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a machinery-hazard/\n  equipment-condition concern (entanglement, crush), ALWAYS escalates\n  immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-materials procurement proposal\n  only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a machine-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Operator unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered operator (crew member) record\n   (`:no-operator`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   operator is.\n2. **Plant unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered textile/fur/leather plant/line record\n   (`:no-plant`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates textile/fur/leather machinery itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a machine-operation-execution finalization, a\n   plant-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface an entanglement/crush/equipment-\n  condition observation -- it never resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"textile\", \"fur\", \"leather\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path. `tflcoord.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION\nPHRASES (\"proceed with the machine operation\", \"finalize the machine\noperation\", \"declare the plant safety cleared\", \"override the plant\nsafety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked only\nagainst the proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own generated\ntext), never against raw `:task` input text.\n`tflcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare domain nouns (\"routine textile/fur/\nleather machine task with fabric rolls, fur pelts and leather hides\"),\nasserting none of them ever hard-trip the finalization-scope rule.\nGreen on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8159\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8159` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8159`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 32 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-machine-operation`/`:approve-\n  plant-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate path: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to\n  finalize a machine operation or a plant-safety clearance exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  whose failure mode is entanglement or crush injury, the capability\n  itself must not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"textile\" \"fur\"\n  \"leather\"]`): rejected outright per this task's explicit CRITICAL\n  self-tripping-bug-pattern warning and the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class -- this domain's own vocabulary necessarily discusses fabric/\n  fur/leather material by name to do its logging/scheduling job, so a\n  bare-noun list would self-block the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  whenever a task description mentions those materials.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:plater-id`/`:tanner-id` (matching the\n  cloud-itonami-isco-8122 reference's own field-naming convention,\n  which explicitly avoided the word \"operator\" to prevent collision\n  with \"operator\" meaning the deploying business/entity): rejected in\n  favor of `:operator-id`/`:plant-id`, matching this task's own\n  domain-design instructions (\"operator/plant record must be\n  independently verified/registered\") and the already-landed sibling\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8132` (Photographic Products Machine Operators,\n  same broad \"machine operators\" occupation family), whose test suite\n  already established `:no-operator`/`:no-plant` as the HARD-check\n  rule names for this ISCO-08 8xxx \"machine operators\" naming\n  convention -- consistency across the sibling family outweighs the\n  8122 ADR's narrower naming-collision concern.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting tflcoord.actor-test\n\nTesting tflcoord.governor-test\n\nRan 32 tests containing 69 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :test/counts "{:total 32, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Textile, Fur and Leather Products Machine Operators Not Elsewhere Classified Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-verification :plant-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :machine-operation-execution-plant-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8159", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8159", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8159], :test/simulator :tflcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8159 \u2014 Textile, Fur and Leather Products Machine Operators Not Elsewhere Classified Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8159}]